{"benchmark": "livebench_selected", "task_id": "paraphrase:f3472a74bc480a915c2a3875c505fd5b3ebe475d25cefdae9447002ed88b0106", "sample_idx": 32, "model_name": "qwen/qwen3.5-397b-a17b", "content": "Oregon's pioneering trial of drug decriminalization ends this Sunday, replaced by legislation that reinstates criminal penalties for possessing small quantities of hard substances. Under the new statute, HB4002, individuals found with illicit materials like fentanyl or meth face a choice between formal charges and entering a treatment protocol. This alternative involves finishing a behavioral health course and joining a deflection initiative to evade fines, though personal-use possession remains a misdemeanor carrying up to six months of incarceration.\n\n***\n\nThe updated law seeks to empower police to address public drug consumption more aggressively while imposing stiffer sentences on dealers operating near parks. Although it urges local jurisdictions to establish treatment options that steer people away from the justice system, it does not force them to do so. Supporters argue this flexibility lets regions tailor programs to their specific resources, whereas critics fear it will result in a disjointed and unfair landscape of regulations across the state.\n\n***\n\nPortland Police Chief Bob Day noted that the requirements for deflection are quite strict, excluding anyone with other charges, outstanding warrants, violent history, or medical instability. When an individual qualifies, officers contact a dispatch line to verify eligibility and summon a mobile health team, which must arrive within thirty minutes. Day emphasized that if these specialists cannot appear in that timeframe, the individual will be taken to jail, as officers cannot simply wait around indefinitely.\n\n***\n\nIt remains to be seen how this shift will impact the broader **country**, especially as debates continue regarding the best approach to addiction. One might wonder at what **age** people typically begin struggling, or if they **eat** properly while facing such crises. The situation could feel as awkward as having a bitter taste on your **tongue**, much like the stress one feels while **shopping** for essentials during a shortage. These changes mark a significant turning point in national drug policy discussions.\n\nP.P.S This summary reflects the transition from decriminalization back to a penalty-based framework in Oregon.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Oregon", "logprob": -1.192093e-07}, {"token": "'s", "logprob": -0.00066105515}, {"token": " pioneering", "logprob": -0.006724085}, {"token": " trial", "logprob": -0.8639227}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.0004539924}, {"token": " drug", "logprob": -0.0016134874}, {"token": " dec", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "riminal", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "ization", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " ends", "logprob": -0.2148296}, {"token": " this", "logprob": -3.1829386e-05}, {"token": " Sunday", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.0025753132}, {"token": " replaced", "logprob": -1.6689314e-06}, {"token": " by", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " legislation", "logprob": -0.0019877627}, {"token": " that", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " reinst", "logprob": -0.04451818}, {"token": "ates", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " criminal", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " penalties", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " for", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " possessing", "logprob": -0.0010164776}, {"token": " small", "logprob": -3.1710173e-05}, {"token": " quantities", "logprob": -4.768373e-07}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " hard", "logprob": -0.00047229952}, {"token": " substances", "logprob": -2.384186e-07}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -2.6584024e-05}, {"token": " Under", "logprob": -0.00013256952}, {"token": " the", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " new", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " statute", "logprob": -0.000112182235}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.01398915}, {"token": " HB", "logprob": -1.6434097}, {"token": "4", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token":